understanding subtraction of matrices is  very easy because it's pretty similar to  addition of matrices the rule to check  if subtraction is possible is exactly  the same as the rule for addition of  matrices two matrices can be subtracted  only if they are of the same order yes  they have to be of the same order  if not then subtraction is not possible  we'll understand this better with a  couple of examples the first matrix we  have is one for in one row and the  second matrix we have is two three in  one row is this subtraction possible I  am NOT asking you to subtract the two  matrices I am just asking you if it's  possible to subtract this matrix from  this one to know if they can be  subtracted we need to know the order of  each pause the video and find the orders  the first matrix has one row and two  columns its order will be 1 by 2 and as  the second matrix also has just one row  and two columns its order will also be 1  by 2 because the order is the same  subtraction is possible here the second  Matrix can be subtracted from the first  one but how do we subtract now if we  assume this to be a minus B we need to  subtract elements of B from the  corresponding elements of a 1 &amp; 2 are  corresponding elements 4 &amp; 3 are  corresponding elements what will be the  elements of the resulting matrix then  the 1 1 at element will be 1 minus 2  element of a minus the corresponding  element of B and the one 2f element will  be 4 minus 3 now we just find these two  elements to get the resulting matrix 1  minus 2 is minus 1 so we write minus 1  as the 1 1 at element 4 minus 3 is 1  which becomes the 1 to earth element  this is our answer minus 1 1  notice that the order of the resulting  matrix is also one by two the order of  the resulting matrix will always be the  same as the order of the two matrices in  question let's look at one more question  now subtract this matrix from this one  try it out to know if this matrix can be  subtracted from this one we first need  to find the orders of each the first  matrix has 2 rows and 2 columns its  order will be 2 by 2 and the second  Matrix has 2 rows and 1 column order  will be 2 by 1 the orders are not the  same which means they cannot be  subtracted so remember before performing  the operation check if they are  compatible for subtraction and only if  they have the same orders we move on to  subtracting the elements of one matrix  from the corresponding elements of the  other  [Music]
 

